-- Rock compressibility by PVT region in a compositional run.  A row of 30 cells
-- holds oil of three components (CO2, methane, decane) and water, with the same
-- water in both PVT regions.  The ROCK record of region 1 (cells 1-15) has no
-- compressibility, and that of region 2 (cells 16-30) a compressibility of
-- 5E-4 /bar; both take 150 bar as the reference pressure.  There are no wells:
-- region 1 starts at 170 bar and region 2 at 130 bar, so the pressure evens out.
--
-- The pore volume of each cell follows the rock compressibility of its region.
-- As region 2 fills, its pores expand and take up more of the fluid, so the
-- pressure evens out at about 138.5 bar rather than the 149.4 bar that rock
-- without compressibility would give.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUNSPEC
------------------------------------------------------------------------
TITLE
   COMPOSITIONAL TWO ROCK COMPRESSIBILITY REGIONS

METRIC

TABDIMS
1* 2 /
OIL
GAS
WATER
DIMENS
30 1 1
/

COMPS
3 /

FULLIMP /

START
  1 'JAN' 2016  /

REGDIMS
1 1 0 0 /

UNIFIN
UNIFOUT

------------------------------------------------------------------------
GRID
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INIT

DX
30*10
/
DY
30*1
/
DZ
30*1
/
TOPS
30*0
/
-- Low enough for the pressures to even out over the first report steps.
PERMX
30*10
/
PERMY
30*10
/
PERMZ
30*10
/
PORO
30*0.1
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROPS
------------------------------------------------------------------------

CNAMES
CO2
METHANE
DECANE
/

EOS
PR /

BIC
0
0
0
/

ACF
0.22394 0.01142 0.4884
/

PCRIT
73.773
45.992
21.03
/

TCRIT
304.128
190.564
617.7
/

MW
44.00
16.04
142.28
/

VCRIT
0.09412
0.09863
0.60980
/

SGFN
0.0 0.00 0.0
0.1 0.00 0.0
0.2 0.05 0.0
0.4 0.10 0.0
0.6 0.40 0.0
0.8 0.60 0.0
0.99 0.70 0.0
/

SWFN
0.01 0.0  0.0
0.20 0.00 0.0
0.40 0.01 0.0
0.60 0.20 0.0
0.80 0.80 0.0
1.00 1.00 0.0
/

SOF3
0.0 0.00 0.0
0.1 0.00 0.0
0.2 0.05 0.05
0.4 0.10 0.10
0.6 0.40 0.40
0.8 0.60 0.60
0.99 0.70 0.70
/

STCOND
15.0 1.0 /

-- One record per PVT region.
ROCK
    150.0  0.0 /
    150.0  5.0E-4 /

PVTW
    75.0  1.03  4.0E-5  0.3  0.0 /
    75.0  1.03  4.0E-5  0.3  0.0 /

DENSITY
    800.0  1000.0  1.0 /
    800.0  1000.0  1.0 /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
REGIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------

PVTNUM
15*1 15*2
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SOLUTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Region 1 starts 20 bar above and region 2 20 bar below the rock reference
-- pressure, so the fluids flow across the region boundary.
PRESSURE
15*170. 15*130.
/
SGAS
30*0.0
/
SWAT
30*0.5
/
TEMPI
30*150
/
ZMF
30*0.05
30*0.15
30*0.80
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------------------
ALL

-- Block values at either end and on either side of the region boundary.
BPR
1 1 1 /
15 1 1 /
16 1 1 /
30 1 1 /
/

BOSAT
1 1 1 /
15 1 1 /
16 1 1 /
30 1 1 /
/

BWSAT
1 1 1 /
15 1 1 /
16 1 1 /
30 1 1 /
/

BDENO
1 1 1 /
15 1 1 /
16 1 1 /
30 1 1 /
/

BDENW
1 1 1 /
15 1 1 /
16 1 1 /
30 1 1 /
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCHEDULE
------------------------------------------------------------------------

RPTRST
BASIC=1
PRESSURE
SGAS
SOIL
SWAT
XMF
YMF
ZMF
DENO
DENG
DENW
VGAS
VOIL
VWAT
KRO
KRG
KRW
/

TSTEP
0.1 0.4 0.5 1.0 1.0 2.0
10*2.5
/
END
